            "review_text": "NottinghamRed\nHockley Heath, United Kingdom1309 contributions\n0\nWe were the only ones there\nJan 2018 • Couples\nRecommended by our Exo Travel Rep as they use this restaurant for cookery class tours, we asked for a table to be booked for us and went along. We were shown to our table by a young girl who had limited English and saw only one other person the whole evening - a young lad that came in and went upstairs to what I presume was the kitchen and then wandered back outside again. We had the honey chicken having read about it on TA but this was thigh chicken and most of the flavour was on the skin which I don't often eat so lacking in taste for me. Had sticky rice which was okay but nothing special. We had spring rolls to start - a few small pieces in very nice sauce though. Finished with banana fritters which were lovely - in syrup with peanuts. Whole meal was 410,000 VD. There was no atmosphere and the girl spent the whole night on her mobile phone texting and talking. We were there about an hour and were really disappointed.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 19, 2018",
