            "review_title": "Review at Anh Tuyet",
            "review_text": "chefkev1\nLos Angeles, California12 contributions\n0\nRestoring the old Vietnam culinary culture\nDec 2017 • Friends\nAfter I was reminded of this hidden gem from the 2001 feature on A Bourdain I lucked out to be staying just a few blocks away. We went for an early dinner and expressed our interest in meeting Madam Tuyêt who joined us with her daughter. She invited us back for a special lunch the following day and that evening I went in to learn several dishes which was a highlight of 10days in Vietnam \n\nTwo weeks earlier Madam Tuyêt had been in Da Nang to prepare the meals for 21 presidents and leaders attending the 2017 APAC meetings. She was a gracious host and wonderful chef who delighted us with stories of her past and some of the finest Vietnamese cuisine. \n\nI was so pleased to learn how to make President Obama's favorite (and one of ours as well) banana flower salad, and A Bourdain's favorite Madam Tuyêt's roasted honey glazed chicken. This is a true cultural experience and one not to be missed when in Hanoi!\nRead more\nWritten December 4, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
